From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] aboutcomputer: read the build from os-release

get_build_number() probed /boot/olpc_build, then /etc/redhat-release, then
lsb_release. None of those exist on Aspartame, so Settings -> About my
Computer reported

    Build: Not available

on a system whose /etc/os-release says IMAGE_ID=aspartame with an image
version. Telling the user their build is unknown when the machine states it
plainly is a small lie in the one screen whose whole job is identifying the
machine.

Fall back to os-release before giving up. Serial Number and Wireless Firmware
still read "Not available" on a virtual machine, which is honest.

--- a/extensions/cpsection/aboutcomputer/model.py
+++ b/extensions/cpsection/aboutcomputer/model.py
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 import os
 import logging
+import platform
 import subprocess
 from gettext import gettext as _
 import errno
@@ -94,6 +95,22 @@
             build_no = build_no.strip().decode()
 
     if build_no is None or not build_no:
+        # Every modern distribution identifies itself in os-release. Without
+        # this the OLPC and Red Hat specific probes above are the only
+        # sources, so Aspartame reported its build as 'Not available' on a
+        # system that names itself plainly.
+        try:
+            os_release = platform.freedesktop_os_release()
+        except (OSError, ValueError):
+            os_release = {}
+        build_no = (os_release.get('IMAGE_ID') or
+                    os_release.get('PRETTY_NAME') or
+                    os_release.get('NAME'))
+        build_id = os_release.get('IMAGE_VERSION') or os_release.get('BUILD_ID')
+        if build_no and build_id:
+            build_no = '%s %s' % (build_no, build_id)
+
+    if build_no is None or not build_no:
         build_no = _not_available
 
     return build_no
